detection	Execute threat detection with AWF	2026-10-21T16:33:04.5335114Z [engine] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0135oww3fpST7bZWUSuF9Gtq","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"items\":[{\"type\":\"add_labels\",\"labels\":[\"T: bug\",\"C: crash\",\"C: preview style\",\"F: fmtskip\"]},{\"type\":\"add_comment\",\"body\":\"Thanks for the report! This is an automated first-pass triage; a maintainer will make the final call.\\n\\n**Reproduction:** Black 25.9.0 (latest release on the issue date) with `--preview --line-length 88` on the `with open(\\\"file.txt\\\") as f: content = f.read() # fmt: skip` snippet: fails with `Cannot parse: 1:4: with`. The same input without `--preview` exits cleanly, so the input is valid and the failure comes from a preview feature. The `main` commit you mention was not tested, because only PyPI releases can be installed.\\n\\n**Assessment:** This looks like a genuine preview-style bug. The `fix_fmt_skip_in_one_liners` feature appears to mishandle a `# fmt: skip` comment on a one-line compound statement such as `with`. Your note about `async with` and `if` with compound conditions is consistent with this, but I only reproduced the plain `with` case.\\n\\n**Next step:** A maintainer should confirm this against current `main`. It would help to know whether the `async with` and `if` variants fail the same way, and to see their exact input snippets.\\n\\n<sub>black-issue-triage skill v1.0.0 · suggested for maintainers: none</sub>\",\"temporary_id\":\"aw_oD5WVTx7\"}],\"errors\":[]}\n/tmp/threat-detection-reasons.json","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ab3e4f52-3163-43f6-82a2-2456bbd06035","uuid":"4eb87154-e2a8-4a88-976d-889a4dd4f6b1","timestamp":"2026-10-21T16:33:04.529Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\"items\":[{\"type\":\"add_labels\",\"labels\":[\"T: bug\",\"C: crash\",\"C: preview style\",\"F: fmtskip\"]},{\"type\":\"add_comment\",\"body\":\"Thanks for the report! This is an automated first-pass triage; a maintainer will make the final call.\\n\\n**Reproduction:** Black 25.9.0 (latest release on the issue date) with `--preview --line-length 88` on the `with open(\\\"file.txt\\\") as f: content = f.read() # fmt: skip` snippet: fails with `Cannot parse: 1:4: with`. The same input without `--preview` exits cleanly, so the input is valid and the failure comes from a preview feature. The `main` commit you mention was not tested, because only PyPI releases can be installed.\\n\\n**Assessment:** This looks like a genuine preview-style bug. The `fix_fmt_skip_in_one_liners` feature appears to mishandle a `# fmt: skip` comment on a one-line compound statement such as `with`. Your note about `async with` and `if` with compound conditions is consistent with this, but I only reproduced the plain `with` case.\\n\\n**Next step:** A maintainer should confirm this against current `main`. It would help to know whether the `async with` and `if` variants fail the same way, and to see their exact input snippets.\\n\\n<sub>black-issue-triage skill v1.0.0 · suggested for maintainers: none</sub>\",\"temporary_id\":\"aw_oD5WVTx7\"}],\"errors\":[]}\n/tmp/threat-detection-reasons.json","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0135oww3fpST7bZWUSuF9Gtq","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
