verify_outputs	Compare requested and applied safe outputs	2026-10-21T16:33:43.9155763Z   AGENT_OUTPUT: {"items":[{"type":"add_labels","labels":["T: bug","C: crash","C: preview style","F: fmtskip"]},{"type":"add_comment","body":"Thanks for the report! This is an automated first-pass triage; a maintainer will make the final call.\n\n**Reproduction:** Black 25.9.0 (latest release on the issue date) with `--preview --line-length 88` on the `with open(\"file.txt\") as f: content = f.read() # fmt: skip` snippet: fails with `Cannot parse: 1:4: with`. The same input without `--preview` exits cleanly, so the input is valid and the failure comes from a preview feature. The `main` commit you mention was not tested, because only PyPI releases can be installed.\n\n**Assessment:** This looks like a genuine preview-style bug. The `fix_fmt_skip_in_one_liners` feature appears to mishandle a `# fmt: skip` comment on a one-line compound statement such as `with`. Your note about `async with` and `if` with compound conditions is consistent with this, but I only reproduced the plain `with` case.\n\n**Next step:** A maintainer should confirm this against current `main`. It would help to know whether the `async with` and `if` variants fail the same way, and to see their exact input snippets.\n\n<sub>black-issue-triage skill v1.0.0 · suggested for maintainers: none</sub>","temporary_id":"aw_oD5WVTx7"}],"errors":[]}
